import json
R=[
("crucifixion-masaccio",7,0,"Christ hangs on the cross while Mary and John grieve below, and Mary Magdalene kneels with her arms thrown wide. Masaccio painted it around 1426, and the figures have real weight and shadow, a new way of painting that changed art in Florence. He died at only 26."),
("adoration-of-the-magi-angelico",7,0,"The three wise men bring gifts to the baby Jesus in this glowing little picture, which is round like a plate. Fra Angelico, a Dominican friar, began it in about 1430, and Filippo Lippi, who was a young friend, probably finished it."),
("madonna-and-child-angelico",7,0,"Mary holds the Christ Child while saints stand nearby in this fresco by Fra Angelico. He was a friar who painted gentle figures in clear, bright colors, and people later called him Beato, meaning blessed."),
("nativity-campin",7,0,"Mary kneels beside her newborn baby in a Flemish winter landscape, and the whole scene is painted in warm, lifelike detail. Robert Campin, the master of Tournai, painted it around 1430, and it is a fine early example of oil painting in the Netherlands."),
("the-madonna-in-the-church",7,0,"Mary, taller than the building, stands inside a vast Gothic cathedral holding the baby Jesus in her arms. Jan van Eyck painted this tiny panel in about 1430, and the light pouring through the windows is a wonder of early oil painting."),
("the-last-judgment-angelico",7,0,"Angels, saints and blessed souls dance toward heaven on one side, while on the other side sinners are driven toward hell. Fra Angelico painted this scene of Judgment Day in the 1430s for a church in Florence."),
("leal-souvenir",1,0,"A man in a red hat looks out at you from a stone ledge, and his face is painted so carefully you can see the stubble on his chin. Jan van Eyck made this portrait in 1432. The words on the frame mean 'Loyal Remembrance', and nobody knows who the man was."),
("the-just-judges",7,0,"Nine knights ride across the countryside on handsome horses, in this panel that was once part of the huge Ghent Altarpiece. Jan and Hubert van Eyck made the altarpiece, but this panel was stolen in 1934 and has never been found, so this picture is a copy."),
("madonna-of-humility",7,0,"Mary sits on the ground, which was a way of showing she was humble, holding the baby Jesus in her lap. Fra Angelico painted this sweet scene in about 1433 with soft colors and gold."),
("portrait-of-a-man-self-portrait",1,0,"A man in a bright red turban looks out at you with a steady gaze. Jan van Eyck probably painted this portrait of himself in 1433, and there is a motto on the frame that means 'As I can', which is a play on his name."),
("adoration-of-the-magi-verona",7,0,"Kings in gorgeous clothes arrive on horses, camels and leopards to bring gifts to the baby Jesus. Stefano da Verona painted this crowded scene in 1434, in the glittering style called International Gothic."),
("annunciation-triptych",7,0,"The angel Gabriel arrives to tell Mary she will have a baby, in a cozy Flemish room with a bed and a bright window. Rogier van der Weyden painted this triptych, a picture with three panels, in about 1434."),
("arnolfini-portrait",1,0,"A couple in a small bedroom holds hands, and a little dog stands at their feet. Look at the round mirror behind them: it shows the whole room, and two people standing in the door. Jan van Eyck painted this in 1434, and he even wrote on the wall that he was there."),
("coronation-of-the-virgin",7,0,"Christ crowns Mary Queen of Heaven in the middle of a crowd of cheering saints and angels. Fra Angelico painted this sparkling scene in about 1434, with gold and bright blue and pink."),
("annunciation-eyck",7,0,"The angel Gabriel and Mary face each other, and the whole thing is painted to look like carved stone figures. Jan van Eyck made it in about 1435, with tiny, perfect brushstrokes."),
("duran-madonna",7,0,"Mary sits holding the baby Jesus in front of a red cloth, with a book in her hand. Rogier van der Weyden painted this small panel in about 1435, and it is named after a Spanish man who once owned it."),
("portrait-of-a-man-with-a-blue-chaperon",1,0,"A man wears a bright blue headdress called a chaperon and holds a gold ring in his hand. Jan van Eyck painted it in about 1435, and the man may be someone getting engaged."),
("madonna-with-canon-joris-van-der-paele",7,0,"A church official named Joris van der Paele kneels in a white robe, with his glasses in his hand, as saints present him to Mary. Jan van Eyck painted every wrinkle on his face in 1436. The tiny details, like the patterned rug, are amazing."),
("barbadori-altarpiece-and-predella",7,0,"Mary and the baby Jesus sit with saints in a lovely painted room, and a row of small scenes runs along the bottom. Filippo Lippi, a Florentine friar, painted this altarpiece in the 1430s."),
("crucifixion-and-last-judgement-diptych",7,0,"Two small panels show Christ on the cross on one side and Judgment Day on the other, with tiny, detailed figures. This pair is attributed to Jan van Eyck, from about 1437, and it is one of his most dramatic pictures."),
("dresden-triptych",7,0,"Mary and the baby Jesus sit at the center of a three-part picture that folds shut like a tiny door. Jan van Eyck painted it in about 1437, and it was made to be carried and prayed in front of."),
("lucca-madonna",7,0,"Mary sits on a throne, and she feeds the baby Jesus while the cloth behind her glows in rich red. Jan van Eyck painted it in about 1437, and it is named for the Italian city of Lucca where it was once kept."),
("madonna-and-child-enthroned",7,0,"Mary holds the baby Jesus on a throne with a beautiful carved marble frame around them. Filippo Lippi painted this in about 1437, with the tender faces that made him famous."),
("portrait-of-a-princess",1,0,"A young woman in profile wears a fancy red dress, and she is surrounded by butterflies and flowers that look like patterns on a tapestry. Pisanello painted it in about 1437, and she may be Ginevra d'Este or Margherita Gonzaga."),
("saint-barbara",7,0,"A young woman sits quietly with a huge tower behind her and a book in her hand. Jan van Eyck made this drawing in 1437, and it is not a painting but a drawing made with a brush and ink. The tower is Barbara's symbol, because the story says she was locked in one."),
("crucifixion-with-st-dominic-praying",7,0,"Saint Dominic kneels at the foot of the cross, hugging the wood, and gazes at Christ. Fra Angelico painted this fresco in the 1430s for the monks to pray in front of."),
("portrait-of-cardinal-niccolo-albergati",1,0,"A cardinal's face shows every wrinkle and bump, painted in great detail, and he looks tired and clever. Jan van Eyck met him in 1431 and probably drew him from life before painting this portrait in 1438."),
("werl-triptych",7,0,"Saint Barbara reads by the fireplace in a cozy room, with a little towel, a candle and a window onto the street. Robert Campin painted this in 1438, and it is full of ordinary things from a house in Flanders."),
("madonna-at-the-fountain",7,0,"Mary stands holding the baby Jesus in front of a rich red cloth held up by two angels, beside a small fountain. Jan van Eyck painted this tiny picture in 1439, and it is just about as wide as a sheet of paper."),
("portrait-of-margareta-van-eyck",1,0,"A woman in a red headdress looks out calmly, with careful, tiny wrinkles painted around her eyes. Jan van Eyck painted his wife, Margareta, in 1439, and wrote on the frame that he finished it on June 17."),
("annunciation-eyck-3",7,0,"Mary and the angel are painted in shades of gray, as if they were statues, in this narrow panel. Jan van Eyck painted it in about 1440 as one half of a diptych, which is a picture made of two panels."),
("bladelin-triptych",7,0,"A baby lies on the ground, wonderfully lit, while a donor kneels in a cold winter scene with a long road running into the distance. Rogier van der Weyden painted this triptych in about 1440."),
("crucifixion-triptych",7,0,"The cross stands at the center with Mary and Saint John grieving, and on the side panels more saints. Rogier van der Weyden painted this triptych in about 1440, and the faces express deep sadness."),
("madonna-of-the-rose-bower-lochner",7,0,"Mary sits in a garden of roses with the baby Jesus while angels play music and hold up a green cloth behind her. Stefan Lochner painted it in Cologne in about 1440, in a sweet, storybook style."),
("portrait-of-a-young-woman-with-a-winged-bonnet",1,0,"A young woman wears a bonnet that looks like it has wings, and she looks down with her hands pressed together. Rogier van der Weyden painted this portrait in about 1440, and she remains a mystery."),
("the-descent-from-the-cross",7,0,"Friends gently lower Christ's body from the cross, while Mary faints in the same pose as her son. Rogier van der Weyden painted this huge, emotional picture in about 1440, and the figures are as lifelike as actors on a stage."),
("the-fountain-of-life",7,0,"A gleaming fountain stands at the center, with a white lamb on top and a crowd of people gathered around it. This is a workshop copy of a Jan van Eyck painting, and the water means the gift of life."),
("the-seven-sacraments",7,0,"Inside a huge church, scenes show the seven holy ceremonies of the Catholic Church, like baptism, marriage and last rites. Rogier van der Weyden painted this triptych in about 1440, and the crucifixion rises right through the middle."),
("coronation-of-the-virgin-lippi",7,0,"Christ crowns Mary in heaven in this large altarpiece, with crowds of angels, saints and singers all around. Filippo Lippi painted it in 1441, and it includes a self-portrait of the artist in a monk's robe."),
("pieta-weyden",7,0,"Mary holds her dead son's body and weeps, with Mary Magdalene beside her. Rogier van der Weyden painted this sad, quiet scene in about 1441, and many people say it is one of the most moving pictures of the 1400s."),
("portrait-of-lionel-d-este",1,0,"A young prince in a rich blue and gold coat looks off to the side in profile. Pisanello painted Leonello d'Este, the ruler of Ferrara, around 1441, and Pisanello was also famous for making medals."),
("the-virgin-and-child",7,0,"Mary holds the baby Jesus in front of a rich, red cloth. This is a small panel painted in the workshop of Jan van Eyck in about 1441, showing how popular his style had become."),
("miraflores-altarpiece",7,0,"Three small scenes show the life of Mary: her son appearing to her, the Lamentation of Christ and more. Rogier van der Weyden painted this triptych in about 1443, and it was once given to a monastery in Spain."),
("the-last-judgment-beaune-altarpiece",7,0,"The archangel Michael weighs souls in the center as people rise from their graves and are sent up to heaven or down to hell. Rogier van der Weyden painted this huge altarpiece for a hospital in Beaune, France, in 1443."),
("saint-jerome-in-his-study-colantonio",7,0,"Saint Jerome sits at his desk in a cluttered room and pulls a thorn from the paw of a lion who has become his friend. Niccolò Colantonio painted it in 1444, and it has books, a cat and many little details to find."),
("the-miraculous-draft-of-fishes",7,0,"Jesus walks on the water near a boat, with the snowy Mont Blanc in the distance. Konrad Witz painted this in 1444, and it is one of the first paintings of a real landscape, Lake Geneva, in European art."),
("annunciation-with-two-kneeling-donors",7,0,"The angel Gabriel arrives in a graceful garden and room, while two small men kneel at the edge. Filippo Lippi painted it in about 1445, and the two small figures are the people who paid for it."),
("madonna-and-child-with-saints-francis-damian-cosmas-and",7,0,"Mary and the baby Jesus sit in a marble niche, and saints stand around them. Filippo Lippi painted this altarpiece in about 1445 for the Medici family in Florence, and the Medici saints Cosmas and Damian are in it."),
("martelli-annunciation",7,0,"The angel kneels before Mary in a room with a long, receding floor, and a vase of lilies stands nearby. Filippo Lippi painted this in about 1445, and it hangs in the church of San Lorenzo in Florence."),
("santa-lucia-de-magnoli-altarpiece",7,0,"Mary sits under a pink and white arch with the baby Jesus while four saints stand nearby, all bathed in pale daylight. Domenico Veneziano painted it in about 1445, and it is known for its fresh, sunny colors."),
("triptych-with-scenes-from-the-life-of-the-virgin",7,0,"A three-part picture shows the Annunciation, the Visit of Mary to Elizabeth and the Adoration of the Magi. Dieric Bouts painted it around 1445, with rich color and tiny details."),
("virgin-of-the-councillors",7,0,"Mary and the baby Jesus sit on a throne with angels while a group of city councillors from Barcelona kneel beside her. Lluís Dalmau painted it in 1445, and the councillors are painted like real people."),
("portrait-of-a-carthusian",1,0,"A monk in a white robe looks out at you from behind a ledge, and there is a fly painted on the frame. Petrus Christus painted it in 1446, and the fly looks so real you might want to brush it away."),
("the-baptism-of-christ-francesca",7,0,"Jesus stands calmly in a little river while John the Baptist pours water over his head, and a dove floats above. Piero della Francesca painted it in about 1448, and it is famous for its quiet, still look."),
("a-goldsmith-in-his-shop",4,0,"A goldsmith weighs a ring while a young couple chooses jewelry. Petrus Christus painted it in 1449, and a round mirror on the counter shows the street outside, with two men and a falcon."),
("seven-saints",7,0,"Seven saints stand next to one another in this panel, each holding the symbol that helps you recognize them. Filippo Lippi painted this altar panel in about 1449."),
("adoration-of-the-shepherds-mantegna",7,0,"The shepherds kneel in a rocky landscape to see the baby Jesus, in a picture with sharp, strong lines. Andrea Mantegna painted it in about 1450, and it looks almost like a carved relief."),
("annunciation-lippi",7,0,"The angel Gabriel kneels before Mary in a garden and a courtyard painted in clear perspective. Filippo Lippi painted this in about 1450, and the lilies mean that Mary is pure."),
("lamentation-of-christ-weyden",7,0,"Friends gather around Christ's body, and everyone's face is full of grief. Rogier van der Weyden and his workshop painted this about 1450, and the way the faces cry is just like real life."),
("nativity-christus",7,0,"The baby Jesus lies on the ground in a ruined stable, and Mary and Joseph kneel beside him. Petrus Christus painted this in about 1450, and it was probably part of a bigger altarpiece."),
("portrait-of-sigismondo-pandolfo-malatesta",1,0,"A prince in a red hat looks to one side, in profile, with a heavy nose and a stern face. Piero della Francesca painted it in 1450, and Sigismondo was a warlord who ruled the Italian city of Rimini."),
("the-agony-in-the-garden",7,0,"Jesus kneels on a hill at night while his friends sleep nearby and soldiers gather in the distance. Andrea Mantegna painted this in about 1450, and the sharp rocks and golden sunrise make it unforgettable."),
("the-annunciation",7,0,"The angel Gabriel bows before Mary, and a dove and a lily show the miracle. This painting is attributed to Petrus Christus, from about 1450, and it is full of symbols."),
("the-entombment-bouts",7,0,"Friends lay Christ's body in the tomb in a rocky place, with each face showing sorrow. Dieric Bouts painted it in about 1450, and it was done in a thin, watery paint called distemper on linen rather than oil on wood."),
("the-last-judgment-bosch",7,0,"God sits above a mix of fire, monsters and people being tossed into hell. Hieronymus Bosch painted the great triptych of Judgment Day, and it is filled with tiny, strange creatures to find."),
("braque-triptych",7,0,"Three small panels show John the Baptist, Mary Magdalene and John the Evangelist, and a skull stands on the outside when it is closed. Rogier van der Weyden painted this in about 1452, and it is named for a family that owned it."),
("virgin-with-the-child-and-scenes-from-the-life-of-st-an",7,0,"Mary sits holding the baby Jesus in front of a long, curving building, and in the background small scenes show the life of Saint Anne. Filippo Lippi painted this round picture, called a tondo, in about 1452."),
("saint-lawrence-enthroned-with-saints-and-donors",7,0,"Saint Lawrence sits on a throne carrying a gridiron, the thing he is said to have been grilled on, and saints and small donors stand around. Filippo Lippi painted it in 1453."),
("the-altar-of-st-john",7,0,"Three panels tell the story of John the Baptist, from his birth to his baptism of Jesus and his death. Rogier van der Weyden painted this triptych in about 1455."),
("madonna-and-sleeping-child",7,0,"Mary holds her baby close while he sleeps, and her cheek rests near his. Andrea Mantegna painted this in about 1457, and the sleeping baby is a sign of how the story would end."),
("portrait-of-cardinal-ludovico-trevisan",1,0,"A cardinal with a big nose and a strong jaw looks calmly at you. Andrea Mantegna painted it in about 1457, and he made the old man's skin look as real as stone."),
("san-zeno-altarpiece",7,0,"Mary and the baby Jesus sit on a throne under a bower of fruit and flowers, surrounded by angels and saints. Andrea Mantegna painted this altarpiece in 1457 for a church in Verona, and the painted columns blend with the real ones."),
("adoration-in-the-forest",7,0,"The baby Jesus lies on the ground in a dark forest, and Mary, a little John the Baptist and God the Father surround him. Filippo Lippi painted this about 1459, and the dark forest sets off the glow of the baby."),
("agony-in-the-garden",7,0,"Christ kneels on a rocky hill as the sun rises, while his friends sleep and Judas leads soldiers toward him. Giovanni Bellini painted this in about 1459, and the sky is one of the most beautiful in early Italian painting."),
("flagellation-of-christ",7,0,"Christ is whipped in a calm, tidy room on the left, while three men stand and talk in a street on the right. Piero della Francesca painted this puzzle in about 1459, and no one is sure who the three men are."),
("madonna-of-the-zodiac",7,0,"Mary and the baby Jesus sit on a throne under an arch with signs of the zodiac around it. Cosimo Tura painted it in about 1459, in a hard, sharp style that stands out."),
("madonna-and-child",7,0,"Mary holds the baby Jesus in front of a window with a view of a landscape, and angels help hold him up. Filippo Lippi painted this about 1460, and it is among his most loved pictures."),
("madonna-with-child",7,0,"Mary holds the baby Jesus in a soft, round way, with a pale face against a dark background. Antonello da Messina painted it in about 1460, and his style was influenced by Flemish oil painting."),
("madonna-with-the-child",7,0,"Mary holds the baby Jesus tenderly, with her face lowered and a soft, sad look in her eyes. Giovanni Bellini painted it around 1460, and he painted many such Madonnas."),
("medici-madonna",7,0,"Mary holds the baby Jesus in a stone niche, and two little angels stand by her. Rogier van der Weyden painted it in about 1460, and it was possibly made for the Medici family in Florence."),
("polyptych-of-the-misericordia",7,0,"Mary spreads her wide cloak to shelter a group of people kneeling under it, in a many-paneled altarpiece. Piero della Francesca painted it in about 1460, and the people under her cloak are the townspeople who paid for it."),
("portrait-of-a-lady-weyden",1,0,"A young woman with a thin face and a veil looks off to the side with her hands folded. Rogier van der Weyden painted it in about 1460, and her elegant, gentle look made it famous."),
("saint-george",7,0,"A young knight in shining armor stands holding a lance, with a dead dragon at his feet. Andrea Mantegna painted this in about 1460, and the dragon is no bigger than a lizard under the saint's foot."),
("the-crucifixion-with-the-virgin-saint-john-the-baptist-",7,0,"Christ hangs on the cross while Mary, John the Baptist, John the Evangelist and Saint Francis stand around. Paolo Uccello painted it in about 1460, with sharp colors and strange, flat figures."),
("death-of-the-virgin-mantegna",7,0,"The apostles gather around Mary as she lies on her deathbed, with a lake and a bridge visible through the windows. Andrea Mantegna painted it in about 1462, and the view out the window shows his home town of Mantua."),
("madonna-of-the-dry-tree",7,0,"Mary and the baby Jesus stand in front of a dry tree with a small fountain, and angels nearby. Petrus Christus painted it in about 1462, and the dead tree is a sign that Christ will bring new life."),
("dance-of-the-death",9,0,"Skeletons lead people of every kind, from emperors to peasants, in a long dance to the grave. Bernt Notke painted it for a church in Lübeck, Germany, in 1463, and the message is that everyone is equal in the end."),
("triptych-the-last-supper",7,0,"Jesus and his friends sit at a table in a modern-looking room, as he breaks the bread. Dieric Bouts painted this big altarpiece in 1464 for a church in Leuven, and it has side panels from the Old Testament."),
("madonna-and-child-with-an-angel",7,0,"Mary holds the baby Jesus, while an angel looks over their shoulders with a long, soft stare. Sandro Botticelli painted this about 1465, when he was a young artist learning from Filippo Lippi."),
("portrait-of-a-lady-baldovinet",1,0,"A woman in profile wears a yellow dress and a veil with a spray of flowers, against a pale blue sky. Alesso Baldovinetti painted it in about 1465, and we do not know who she was."),
("profile-portrait-of-a-young-lady",1,0,"A young woman stands in profile with her hair tied up in a jeweled net and a pearl necklace around her neck. It was painted in Florence around 1465 and is attributed to one of the Pollaiuolo brothers."),
("cardinal-of-portugal-s-altarpiece",7,0,"Three saints stand in a row, with a painted floor of fine marble under their feet. Antonio and Piero del Pollaiuolo painted it in 1467 for a chapel where a young cardinal was buried."),
("madonna-della-loggia",7,0,"Mary holds the baby Jesus on a balcony with a view out to the sky. Sandro Botticelli painted it in 1467, and the baby seems to reach up for his mother's face."),
("madonna-of-the-milk",7,0,"Mary holds the baby Jesus close in a tender pose. Andrea del Verrocchio, who also taught Leonardo da Vinci, painted this around 1467."),
("madonna-and-child-and-two-angels",7,0,"Mary and the baby Jesus sit with two angels in a soft, rounded picture. Sandro Botticelli painted it about 1468, and the angels' long curling hair shows his love of flowing lines."),
("polyptych-of-madonna-and-child-with-saints",7,0,"Mary and the baby Jesus sit in the center of a golden altarpiece, with saints on either side in individual panels. Carlo Crivelli painted it in 1468, and his gold and jewelry are so detailed they look like they could be touched."),
("the-last-judgment",7,0,"A huge triptych shows Judgment Day, with the archangel Michael weighing souls and people rising from their graves. Hans Memling painted it in about 1469, and the Italian ship that carried it to Italy was captured by pirates."),
("adoration-of-the-magi-triptych",7,0,"The three kings bring gifts to the baby Jesus in a crumbling stable, painted on three panels. Hans Memling painted this in about 1470, and it has a gold, red and blue color you can almost feel."),
("apollo-and-daphne",5,0,"The nymph Daphne turns into a tree as the god Apollo chases her, and her fingers sprout leaves. Piero del Pollaiuolo painted this in about 1470, and the story comes from Greek myth."),
("death-of-the-virgin-goes",7,0,"The apostles gather around Mary as she lies on her deathbed, and they are shocked and sad. Hugo van der Goes painted it about 1470, and every face shows a different feeling."),
]
json.dump([list(r) for r in R],open("../out/old_00.json","w"),ensure_ascii=False,indent=0)
print(len(R))
